content.text:
The evidence points to one root fault, with its effect travelling through two services to the user-facing dashboard. The JSON below is the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel2-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, metric, min(value) AS mn, max(value) AS mx, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'ts-travel2-service%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-travel2-service pod restarted once (restarts=1) in the abnormal window; it was 0 in the normal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'normal' AS src, count(*) AS spans FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-travel2-service' UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal', count(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-travel2-service'", "claim": "ts-travel2-service emitted about 1212 spans in the normal period and none in the abnormal period."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message LIKE '%Connection refused%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-route-plan-service logs 503s with 'Connection refused' when calling its travel2 dependency."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name = 'POST /api/v1/travel2service/trips/left' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-ui-dashboard's POST travel2service/trips/left returned 503 on 30 of 36 requests in the abnormal window."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-travel2-service", "to": "ts-route-plan-service", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code = 'Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-route-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND span_name = 'POST' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Half of ts-route-plan-service's outgoing POST calls errored (54 of 108) while travel2 was down."}]},
    {"from": "ts-route-plan-service", "to": "ts-travel-plan-service", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS avg_ms, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code = 'Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-route-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-route-plan-service cheapestRoute/quickestRoute server spans all errored, averaging 4-6 seconds."}, {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS avg_ms, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code = 'Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND span_name = 'POST' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-travel-plan-service's POST calls to route-plan failed, 3 of 11, averaging 16 seconds."}]},
    {"from": "ts-travel-plan-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS avg_ms, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code = 'Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice/travelPlan/cheapest' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "travelPlan/cheapest averages 20-60 seconds at ui-dashboard and travel-plan, with 3 errors at travel-plan."}]},
    {"from": "ts-travel2-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name = 'POST /api/v1/travel2service/trips/left' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Direct user-facing travel2 trips/left requests at ui-dashboard returned 503 on 30 of 36 requests."}]}
  ]
}
```
